          "date": "2026-11-20 04:44:32.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-930 misc: fix file patterns in MAINTAINERS",
        "message": "LU-930 misc: fix file patterns in MAINTAINERS\n\nMany F: patterns in MAINTAINERS match no file on master,\nbecause the files moved or were removed. The\nget_maintainer.pl script then misses those files.\n\nChange the patterns for these moves:\n- Man pages: lustre/doc/ to Documentation/man<N>/.\n- UAPI headers: lustre/include/uapi/ to include/uapi/.\n- User headers: lustre/include/lustre/ to include/lustre/.\n- libcfs: to lnet/libcfs/, lib/libcfs/, include/libcfs/\n  and include/linux/libcfs/. The compatibility code is\n  now in lustre_compat/ and include/lustre_compat/.\n- Encryption: libcfs crypto to lustre_compat/fs/crypto/.\n- Build: autoconf files to config/, kmp files to rpm/.\n\nFix the patterns for files with a new name or a wrong\nname. These are dt_object.h, range_lock.h,\nliblustreapi_param.c, lsvcgss, obd_sysfs.c,\nlustre_nrs*.h and the pacemaker resource agents. The\nlctl-pcc and lctl-lcfg man pages also change. Remove\nthe patterns for build/ and lustre_patchless_compat.h,\nwhich no longer exist.\n\nAdd the Data-on-MDT code files mdt_io.c and mdc_dev.c,\nand the write barrier code that snapshots use.\n\nEach F: pattern now matches at least 1 file.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: Id0e5f625cafe5f70bf3459caf9390c679b58c6b4\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
